    "description": "Given a string $S$, count the occurrences of each printable non-whitespace character and print the frequency map sorted according to specific precedence rules. Characters must be sorted primarily by their frequency in descending order (highest count first). In the event of a tie where two or more characters appear the exact same number of times, break the tie by sorting the characters in ascending order of their ASCII values. \n\nEach character and its corresponding frequency must be formatted as `c:count` (for instance, `a:3`). Output all unique character-frequency pairs separated by a single space on a single line. Ignore newline (`\\n`), carriage return (`\\r`), and space (` `) characters in the input text. Because there are at most 128 printable ASCII characters, sorting the frequency table requires $O(1)$ operations, resulting in an optimal $O(N)$ overall time complexity.",
