    "description": "Implement the Knuth-Morris-Pratt (KMP) string matching algorithm in C. Given a text string $T$ and a pattern string $P$, determine all 0-based starting indices in $T$ where pattern $P$ appears as an exact match. The standard naive pattern searching algorithm takes $O(|T| \\times |P|)$ worst-case time, which degenerates when many partial matches occur. \n\nThe KMP algorithm achieves optimal $O(|T| + |P|)$ time complexity by preprocessing pattern $P$ into a Longest Prefix Suffix (LPS) array. The LPS array `lps[i]` stores the length of the longest proper prefix of $P[0..i]$ that is also a suffix of $P[0..i]$. During matching, whenever a character mismatch occurs after several matches, the LPS array informs the search pointer how many characters can be safely skipped without re-evaluating text characters. Output all 0-based match indices separated by a space, or `-1` if pattern $P$ does not occur in $T$.",
