    "description": "### Problem Statement\nYou are given two non-empty linked lists representing two non-negative integers. The digits are stored in **reverse order**, such that the 1's digit is at the head of the list. Each of their nodes contains a single digit ($0-9$). Add the two numbers and return the sum as a linked list in the same reverse digit format.\n\n#### Mathematical Logic:\nJust like column addition by hand:\n- Sum the corresponding digits of both lists along with any `carry` from the previous position:\n  $$\\text{total} = \\text{val}_1 + \\text{val}_2 + \\text{carry}$$\n- The new node value is $\\text{total} \\% 10$.\n- The new carry is $\\lfloor \\text{total} / 10 \\rfloor$.\n- Continue while list 1 has nodes, list 2 has nodes, or `carry > 0`.\n\n#### Input & Output:\n- Line 1: $N$ and $M$ (lengths of numbers 1 and 2).\n- Line 2: $N$ space-separated digits for number 1.\n- Line 3: $M$ space-separated digits for number 2.\n- Output: The sum list formatted as `d1 -> d2 -> ... -> NULL`.",
