    "description": "### Problem Statement\nA **Double-Ended Queue (Deque)** is an abstract data type that generalizes both stacks and queues by permitting efficient insertions and deletions at **both the front and back** ends. Deques are essential in sliding window algorithms, work-stealing schedulers, and undo-redo buffers.\n\nImplement a dynamic or circular deque in C with the following specifications:\n\n#### Supported Commands:\n1. `PUSH_FRONT <val>`: Insert integer `<val>` at the front of the deque.\n2. `PUSH_BACK <val>`: Insert integer `<val>` at the back of the deque.\n3. `POP_FRONT`: Remove and print the front element. If empty, print `EMPTY`.\n4. `POP_BACK`: Remove and print the back element. If empty, print `EMPTY`.\n5. `GET_FRONT`: Print the front element without removing it. If empty, print `EMPTY`.\n6. `GET_BACK`: Print the back element without removing it. If empty, print `EMPTY`.\n7. `SIZE`: Print the current number of elements in the deque.\n\nEnsure all dynamically allocated memory is cleanly released before program exit.",
